The code statements that lead to the bug are:
isert_conn->login_req_len = wc->byte_len - ISER_HEADERS_LEN;
Reason:
The subtraction is performed without verifying that wc->byte_len is at least ISER_HEADERS_LEN, causing a signed integer underflow to a negative value. This negative length is later used as a memcpy size, leading to an out-of-bounds write.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (unlikely(wc->byte_len < ISER_HEADERS_LEN)) {
    isert_dbg("login request length %u is too short\n", wc->byte_len);
    return;
}
Reason:
This guards against login PDUs shorter than ISER_HEADERS_LEN, ensuring that the subsequent subtraction always yields a non-negative length and preventing the underflow.

